From: NanoKVM BSP <nanokvm@local>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: mm: export arch_sync_dma_for_{device,cpu}

The CVITek multimedia modules do their own cache maintenance against physical
addresses: sys_cache_flush()/sys_cache_invalidate() in cv181x_sys and the CMDQ
path in cv181x_vpss call arch_sync_dma_for_device() directly. Ten call sites
across the stack, all physical-address based.

Nothing exported does the same job. The dma_sync_single_for_*() API needs a
struct device and a dma_addr_t, which these paths do not carry -- the buffers
come from the ION carveout as bare physical addresses.

Export the two DMA cache hooks so the modules can be built out-of-tree. This
is deliberately narrow: it exposes existing arch functionality that is already
called from any driver using the streaming DMA API, and adds no new behaviour.

Signed-off-by: NanoKVM BSP <nanokvm@local>
---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/mm/dma-noncoherent.c b/arch/riscv/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
index cb89d7e0ba88..be784b34cc81 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ void arch_sync_dma_for_device(phys_addr_t paddr, size_t size,
 		break;
 	}
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(arch_sync_dma_for_device);
 
 void arch_sync_dma_for_cpu(phys_addr_t paddr, size_t size,
 			   enum dma_data_direction dir)
@@ -113,6 +114,7 @@ void arch_sync_dma_for_cpu(phys_addr_t paddr, size_t size,
 		break;
 	}
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(arch_sync_dma_for_cpu);
 
 void arch_dma_prep_coherent(struct page *page, size_t size)
 {
